# Katherine DeMay
My name is Katherine DeMay, and I am a sophomore at Oregon State University pursuing a double degree in Biology and Data Science with a concentration in Life Sciences. My interest in data science stems from my passion for working with numbers, organizing information, and analyzing data and solving problems. Through my coursework, I have been developing skills in research, data collection, data management, and statistical analysis, with a particular focus on applications within the life sciences. I am especially interested in how data can be used to drive scientific discoveries and help our understanding of biological systems and processes.By combining my backgrounds in biology and data science, I hope to bridge the gap between scientific research and data-driven decision-making. After graduation, I plan to pursue a career in drug discovery or the pharmaceutical industry, where I can apply data analytics to support innovative research and contribute to the development of new medicines and treatments. I am excited to continue expanding my knowledge, refining my technical skills, and gaining hands-on experience in this rapidly growing field.
